SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] John G. Pappas v. Stephen H. Leask d/b/a Sout
 hgate Restaurant
DESCRIPTION:1  \nSTATE OF MAINE BUSINESS AND CONSUMER COURT  Cumberland\, 
 ss. Location:  Portland  Docket No.:  BCD-CV-15-07   JOHN G. PAPPAS\,  Pla
 intiff\,  v.  STEVEN H.  LEASK  d/b/a Southgate Restaurant\,  Defendant.  
   \n) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) ) )  \n       \nDECISION AND JUDGMENT  Plaintiff Joh
 n Pappas has brought this action against Defendant Steven Leask\, doing bu
 siness as Southgate Restaurant\, seeking damages for employment discrimina
 tion in violation of the Maine Human Rights Act.  A trial was held Februar
 y 24\, 2016 through February 26\, 2016.  By agreement of the parties\, wit
 nesses other than the parties were sequestered throughout the trial.  Afte
 r the trial\, the parties submitted proposed findings of fact and conclusi
 ons of law.    Based on the entire record\, the court hereby adopts the fi
 ndings and conclusions set forth below\, and grants judgment to Defendant.
  1.   Steven H. Leask has worked as a machinist for Bath Iron Works (BIW) 
 for many years.  For many years\, the Southgate Restaurant has been a loca
 lly owned restaurant serving breakfast and lunch at its location in Bath\,
  near the BIW facility.  Mr. Leask was a frequent diner at Southgate befor
 e 2006.  In that year\, after learning \n2  \nthat the owners were plannin
 g to close the restaurant\, Mr. Leask purchased it in his own name.   2. H
 e has had no training or experience in operating any business\, including 
 a restaurant\, and he did not give up his job at BIW after making the purc
 hase—his purpose in buying Southgate was simply to keep the restaurant o
 pen.   The purchase was a turnkey transaction\, and Mr. Leask changed very
  little after the purchase.  Mr. Leask runs the restaurant very informally
 .  His involvement in day-to-day restaurant operations has been limited to
  coming in around the 2 p.m. closing time\, to tally the restaurant’s re
 ceipts for the day.  3. Responsibility for the daily operation of the rest
 aurant rests mainly with the restaurant manager\, Doreen Beaulieu\, who al
 so is Mr. Leask’s domestic partner.   The othe\nhttps://www.courts.maine
 .gov/courts/bcd/cv-orders/CV-15-07/CV-15-07%20Pappas%20v%20Leask%20Decisio
 n.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/courts/bcd/cv-orders/CV-15-07/CV-15-07%20
 Pappas%20v%20Leask%20Decision.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
